.TH DEXDECK 1 "July 2026" "DexDeck 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dexdeck \- private terminal control plane for Android development
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dexdeck
[GLOBAL OPTIONS] [COMMAND [OPTIONS]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
DexDeck models Android Gradle projects and provides build, run, test, device,
emulator, task, diagnostic, and Logcat operations through a CLI and TUI.
It contains no telemetry or direct network client.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --project " PATH"
Select an Android project root or nested project path.
.TP
.BI --module " GRADLE_PATH"
Select an exact Android module.
.TP
.BI --variant " NAME"
Select an exact enabled variant.
.TP
.BI --device " SERIAL_OR_SELECTOR"
Select an exact device or configured selector.
.TP
.BI --format " human|json|jsonl"
Select output contract. Status remains on standard error.
.SH COMMANDS
init, doctor, project, modules, variants, devices, emulators, build, install, launch,
run, rerun, reinstall, clean-reinstall, stop, uninstall, clear-data, test, logs,
gradle, emulator, command, and version.
.SH FILES
.I .dexdeck/config.toml
is optional shared project configuration. User configuration, cache, session,
jobs, filters, and trust state use platform-standard private directories.
.SH PRIVACY
No analytics, telemetry, uploads, update checks, or direct HTTP requests. Raw
logs are persisted only after explicit export or recording actions.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project documentation at https://github.com/drilonrecica/dexdeck.
